<setup>
<selectFromSequence name="a" from="2" to="5"/>
<selectFromSequence name="c" from="-3" to="3" exclude="$a 0"/>
<function name="f">
    $a*x - x^2
  </function>
  <derivative name="fP">$f</derivative>
  <number name="coeff">$a-2$c</number>
<math name="coeffh" simplify>($a-2$c)h</math>
</setup>

  <p>
    Consider the function <m>f(x) = $f</m>.  We are going to use the limit definition of the derivative to determine <m>f'($c)</m>.

    <ol marker="a.">
      <li>
        <p>
          Recall that the limit definition of <m>f'($c)</m> is
          <me> f'($c) = \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{f($c+h)-f($c)}{h} </me>
          and thus we need to determine expressions for <m>f($c+h)</m> and <m>f($c+h) - f($c)</m>.
        </p>

        <p>Using the given formula <m>f(x) = $f</m>,
      which of the following is the simplest possible expression for <m>f($c+h)</m>?
            <answer>
              <choiceInput><shortDescription>Pick the simplest expression.</shortDescription>
                <choice><m>f($c+h) = $a($c+h)-($c+h)^2 </m></choice>
                <choice><m>f($c+h)=  <math simplify> -h^2 +  $c($a-$c) + $a*h </math></m>  </choice>
                <choice><m>f($c+h)=  <math simplify> h^2 +  $c($a-$c) + ($a-2$c)*h </math></m>  </choice>
                <choice credit="1"><m>f($c+h)=  <math simplify> -h^2 + $c($a-$c) + ($a-2$c)*h </math></m>  </choice>
              </choiceInput>
            </answer>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
      <p>Which of the following is the simplest possible expression for <m>f($c+h) - f($c)</m>?
            <answer>
              <choiceInput><shortDescription>Pick the simplest expression.</shortDescription>
                <choice><m>f($c+h) - f($c) = $a($c+h)-($c+h)^2 <math simplify>-$$f($c)</math> </m></choice>
                <choice><m>f($c+h) - f($c) = <math simplify> - h^2 + $a*h </math></m>  </choice>
                <choice credit="1"><m>f($c+h)  - f($c) = <math simplify>  -h^2 +  ($a-2$c)*h </math></m>  </choice>
                <choice><m>f($c+h) - f($c) =  <math simplify> h^2 + ($a-2$c)*h </math></m>  </choice>
              </choiceInput>
            </answer>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Next, apply the limit definition of the derivative by substituting the simplest possible expression for <m>f($c+h)-f($c)</m> in the space provided:
        </p>
        <p>
      <answer><mathInput name="dq_x1" prefill="/h" minWidth="20"><label><m>f'($c)= \displaystyle \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{f($c+h)-f($c)}{h} = \lim_{h \to 0} </m> </label><description>Simplify the numerator.</description></mathInput>
        <award symbolicEquality simplifyOnCompare="normalizeOrder">
          <when>$dq_x1 = (-h^2 +  $coeffh)/h
      </when></award>
        <award credit="0" name="notsimplified" symbolicEquality simplifyOnCompare="full" expandOnCompare><when>$dq_x1 =
        ($$f($c+h) - $$f($c))/h
      </when></award>
        <award credit="0" name="toosimplified"><when>$dq_x1 =
        ($$f($c+h) - $$f($c))/h
      </when></award>
      </answer></p>
        <feedback condition="$notsimplified">Your numerator is not simplified enough, yet.</feedback>
        <feedback condition="$toosimplified">Don't divide by <m>h</m> until the next answer box. Leave this answer with a numerator divided by <m>h</m>.</feedback>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Further, factoring the numerator and simplifying the quotient as much as possible, we see that</p>
        <p>
      <answer><mathInput name="simp_x1"><label><m>f'($c)= \displaystyle \lim_{h \to 0} </m> </label></mathInput>
        <award symbolicEquality simplifyOnCompare="normalizeOrder"><when>$simp_x1 = -h + $coeff
      </when></award>
        <award credit="0" name="notsimplified2" symbolicEquality simplifyOnCompare="full" expandOnCompare><when>$simp_x1 =
        ($$f($c+h) - $$f($c))/h
      </when></award></answer></p>
        <feedback condition="$notsimplified2">Your answer is not simplified enough, yet.</feedback>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Finally, evaluating the limit by letting <m>h \to 0</m>, we determine the value of <m>f'($c)</m>:</p>
        <p><answer symbolicEquality><label><m>f'($c) = </m> </label>$$fP($c)</answer></p>
      </li>

    </ol>
  </p>